 "code": null,
 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>In RMI, the <b>server</b> creates and offers a remote object, and the <b>client</b> finds that object and calls its methods.</p><table><tr><th>Server role</th><th>Client role</th></tr><tr><td>Creates the remote object</td><td>Looks up the object in the RMI registry</td></tr><tr><td>Exports it (UnicastRemoteObject)</td><td>Gets a stub (proxy) for it</td></tr><tr><td>Registers it with a name (bind/rebind)</td><td>Calls remote methods on the stub</td></tr><tr><td>Waits for calls and runs methods</td><td>Receives results or RemoteException</td></tr></table>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Who registers the object in the registry?",
  "options": [
   "Client",
   "Server"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "Cows Eat Roses: Register = server."
 }
